WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.700
The person in the water turned out to be a boy.

2
00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:09.966
He was holding a large basket of mud.

3
00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:15.357
Coughing, Vinnie climbed back onto the tiny island.

4
00:00:15.358 --> 00:00:18.601
"Who are you?" the boy asked.

5
00:00:18.602 --> 00:00:22.242
"I’m Vinnie. This is my sister, Mandy,"

6
00:00:22.243 --> 00:00:27.613
Vinnie replied, shaking his wet hair.

7
00:00:27.614 --> 00:00:31.982
"Where is your family garden?" the boy asked.

8
00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:36.224
"We don’t have one," admitted Vinnie.

9
00:00:36.225 --> 00:00:37.875
"We’re just visiting.

10
00:00:37.876 --> 00:00:40.227
Do you need help?"

11
00:00:40.228 --> 00:00:42.831
The boy thought a moment.

12
00:00:42.832 --> 00:00:45.216
"Yes," he said.

13
00:00:45.217 --> 00:00:47.324
"Collect mud from the lake.

14
00:00:47.325 --> 00:00:49.670
Then pile it on here."

15
00:00:49.671 --> 00:00:53.304
He pointed to the island.

16
00:00:53.305 --> 00:00:57.074
He had dark skin and was dressed like Vinnie.

17
00:00:57.075 --> 00:01:01.080
"Why do you need mud?" Vinnie asked.

18
00:01:01.081 --> 00:01:04.421
The boy looked at them, surprised.

19
00:01:04.422 --> 00:01:08.206
"It helps the crops grow strong," he said.

20
00:01:08.207 --> 00:01:11.418
"Corn and beans grow best on this soil.

21
00:01:11.419 --> 00:01:14.411
Our corn was very good last year.

22
00:01:14.412 --> 00:01:18.556
So we are making more floating gardens."

23
00:01:18.557 --> 00:01:21.175
"What a great name!"

24
00:01:21.176 --> 00:01:23.275
Mandy clapped her hands.

25
00:01:23.276 --> 00:01:27.557
The tiny islands did look like floating gardens.

26
00:01:27.558 --> 00:01:30.217
Each one had a different crop.

27
00:01:30.218 --> 00:01:36.559
For the next hour, Vinnie and Mandy helped the boy.

28
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.467
They piled mud on the island.

29
00:01:39.468 --> 00:01:42.402
Mandy smoothed the mud with a stick.

30
00:01:42.403 --> 00:01:44.809
A canoe went by.

31
00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.871
"Look, Vinnie!" she called.

32
00:01:47.872 --> 00:01:53.860
"People use canoes to move from one island to the next."

33
00:01:53.861 --> 00:01:58.161
"Who are you, little girl?" someone behind her asked.

34
00:01:58.162 --> 00:02:00.406
Mandy turned around.

35
00:02:00.407 --> 00:02:05.016
A man was sitting in a canoe with a big pile of

36
00:02:05.017 --> 00:02:07.083
corn. He had kind

37
00:02:07.084 --> 00:02:10.683
eyes. "We’re friends of . . ." Mandy

38
00:02:10.684 --> 00:02:14.888
paused. She didn’t know the boy’s

39
00:02:14.889 --> 00:02:17.678
name. "Of Mazatl? I

40
00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:20.751
see. Where is my son now?" he

41
00:02:20.752 --> 00:02:25.473
asked. "He’s getting mud from the water, sir," she

42
00:02:25.474 --> 00:02:30.268
replied. Mandy thought Mazatl looked very much like his

43
00:02:30.269 --> 00:02:33.671
father. "Good," Mazatl’s father

44
00:02:33.672 --> 00:02:36.334
nodded. "Tell Mazatl I will be at the

45
00:02:36.335 --> 00:02:39.550
market. I want to go early to get a good

46
00:02:39.551 --> 00:02:41.972
spot." He paddled

47
00:02:41.973 --> 00:02:45.369
away. As Mandy watched him leave, she

48
00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:47.950
wondered, "Where are

49
00:02:47.951 --> 00:02:53.872
we?" When the boys returned, Mandy told Mazatl what his father

50
00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:58.936
said. "I must hurry and join Papa at the weekly market," said

51
00:02:58.937 --> 00:03:02.576
Mazatl. "May we come with you?" asked

52
00:03:02.577 --> 00:03:06.614
Vinnie. "Yes, but come to my house first," said

53
00:03:06.615 --> 00:03:11.487
Mazatl. "We can take a bath and change our

54
00:03:11.488 --> 00:03:14.545
clothes." "Thanks, Mazatl," Mandy

55
00:03:14.546 --> 00:03:17.875
said. "What a great place this

56
00:03:17.876 --> 00:03:19.590
is." Mazatl

57
00:03:19.591 --> 00:03:23.251
